{#- The waitlist's form: one field and the call to action (targum-internal#69).

    A plain post to `/waitlist`, which answers with a page of its own, so it works with
    JavaScript off and from any page it stands on. Drawn on the landing twice and on
    every page in front of the door that sells (2026-09-27). `note` adds the line under
    it that says what happens next.

    The action carries the language the visitor pressed, so the answer, the mail and the
    invitation are in it (targum-internal#391). Where nothing was pressed the browser
    decides, at the post as it did on the page. -#}
<form class="join-form" method="post" action="/waitlist{% if asked|default('') %}?lang={{ asked }}{% endif %}">
  <label class="field">
    <input type="email" name="email" required inputmode="email" autocapitalize="off" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="email" placeholder="{{ t("landing.page.you-example-com", "you@example.com") }}" aria-label="{{ t("landing.page.your-email", "Your email") }}">
    <button class="btn cta" type="submit">{{ t("landing.page.join-the-waitlist", "Join the waitlist") }}</button>
  </label>
  {%- if note|default(false) %}
  <p class="join-note">{{ t("landing.page.we-re-opening-in-small-groups-we-ll", "We’re opening in small groups. We’ll email you when your turn comes.") }}</p>
  {%- endif %}
</form>
